Can you only gain one level of experience at a time, for killing any
one monster?
I found a sink on dungeon level one, and by quaffing got polymorphed
into a cockatrice. Went down a level, found a shop (closed for
inventory, ha ha, even better) kicked the door in and when the
shopkeeper attacked he turned to stone. I expected to gain a large
number of experience points and go up several levels from level one.
However, I only got the message "Welcome to experience level 2".
Not fair I reckon'. Still, it was nice to have a free shopfull of
goodies.
Despite this, I had a typically unlucky nethack death.
When I reverted to human form (Samurai), I tried to put my armour back
on, but hit P (put on) instead of W (wear). Instead of armor I put on
a square amulet I had just picked up. It was a cursed amulet of
strangulation. All I could do was pray, (not having any scrolls of
remove curse), and sure enough, my god refused to help because he was
pissed off at me killing the shopkeeper.
Goodbye, Samurai. (hey, what a great song title).

